Assertion Passes when <code>visible()</code> the view is rendered (<code>Visibility::VISIBLE</code>) <code>notVisible()</code> the view is not rendered (<code>INVISIBLE</code> or <code>GONE</code>) <code>gone()</code> <code>Visibility::GONE</code>: not rendered and occupies no space <code>text("...")</code> the text of the view equals the string <p>These visibility assertions are the ones that see invisible views; every other assertion works on visible views only.</p> <p>The following test checks that the label stays hidden until the button is clicked:</p> <pre><code>TEST_F(UIClick, HelloAppearsAfterClick) {
    EXPECT_CALL(*mTestWindow, onButtonClicked).Times(1);
    // press the button
    By::text("Say hello").perform(click());

    // check label is appeared
    By::text("Hello!").check(visible(), "label is not appeared");
}
</code></pre> <p>To check something that has no assertion (a state of a view), cast the view and use the GTest macros:</p> <pre><code>auto field = _cast&lt;ATextField&gt;(By::name("#username").one());
ASSERT_TRUE(field);
EXPECT_EQ(field-&gt;getText(), "Steve");
</code></pre>
